From e0c74534c882b93b3149edb1e4e5b73533d40f62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Michal=20Brng=C3=A1l?= <michal@brngal.sk>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 10:39:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tests: the new http tests use the http
 ServerClientTestCase.inc

The GHSA-pcmh, GHSA-52jp and GHSA-hgf5 tests come from branches whose
openssl ServerClientTestCase.inc supports ephemeral ports
(phpt_notify_server_start()). 7.2's does not, so they include the copy
in ext/standard/tests/http that came with the GHSA-v8xr fix. Test
change only.

Sury's 7.2 patch 0184.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
